      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "By the residue theorem (see "
        },
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "a",
          "attributes": [
            [
              "href",
              "#thm-residue"
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "), the contour integral can be evaluated. Combined with the Bernstein expansion ("
        },
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "a",
          "attributes": [
            [
              "href",
              "#bernstein-exp"
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "), this yields the bound."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "A stronger result follows from the triangle inequality ("
        },
        {
          "kind": "element",
          "name": "a",
          "attributes": [
            [
              "href",
              "#triangle-ineq"
            ]
          ],
          "children": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "text": "3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": ") applied to the decomposition below."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h3",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Theorem 1 (Residue Theorem)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "For any meromorphic function f and a contour C..."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "h3",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Lemma 2 (Bernstein Expansion)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Let P be a polynomial of degree n. Then for any z with |z| = 1..."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "ul",
